Feature: Stream patient data real-time from Purgo S3 location into patient_data_auto_loader table

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the access key and secret key are retrieved securely from the Databricks secret scope "aws_keys"

  Scenario: Retrieve S3 folder path from ingest_config_master table
    Given the source object name contains the keyword "patient_data"
    When retrieving the S3 folder path from the "s3_landing_path" column of the "ingest_config_master" table
    Then the S3 folder path is retrieved successfully

  Scenario Outline: Stream patient data from S3 into patient_data_auto_loader table
    Given the S3 folder path is retrieved from the "s3_landing_path" column of the "ingest_config_master" table
    And the schema location is "/mnt/checkpoints/s3_autoloader/patient_al_schema"
    And the checkpoint location is "/mnt/checkpoints/patient_al_cp/"
    When streaming patient data from the S3 folder path into the "patient_data_auto_loader" table
    Then the patient data is streamed successfully
    And all columns are read as String type, except "data_loaded_at" which is read as a timestamp

    Examples:
      | patient_id | patient_name | age | diagnosis | treatment | data_loaded_at |
      | "12345"    | "John Doe"   | "30" | "Diabetes" | "Medication" | "2022-01-01 12:00:00" |

  Scenario: Handle errors during streaming process
    Given an error occurs during the streaming process
    When handling the error
    Then an error message is displayed
    And the streaming process is stopped

  Scenario: Validate data types of patient data columns
    Given the patient data columns are "patient_id", "patient_name", "age", "diagnosis", "treatment", and "data_loaded_at"
    When validating the data types of the patient data columns
    Then the data types are validated successfully
    And the data types match the expected data types

    Examples:
      | column_name | expected_data_type |
      | "patient_id" | "String"          |
      | "patient_name" | "String"          |
      | "age" | "String"          |
      | "diagnosis" | "String"          |
      | "treatment" | "String"          |
      | "data_loaded_at" | "Timestamp"      |

  Scenario: Validate schema location and checkpoint location
    Given the schema location is "/mnt/checkpoints/s3_autoloader/patient_al_schema"
    And the checkpoint location is "/mnt/checkpoints/patient_al_cp/"
    When validating the schema location and checkpoint location
    Then the schema location and checkpoint location are validated successfully
    And the locations match the expected locations

    Examples:
      | location_type | expected_location |
      | "schema_location" | "/mnt/checkpoints/s3_autoloader/patient_al_schema" |
      | "checkpoint_location" | "/mnt/checkpoints/patient_al_cp/" |
